# will_no_duplicate — a will offers no act twice in a phase, and a second thought goes another way
#
# A will's goal is not chosen, so it never passed the proposal ledger: Bargaining asked about a trader
# twice put the same button on screen twice (a playtest, on a blacksmith's apprentice). Now its ways are
# read through what the ledger leaves. The poultry keeper trades from the coop and stands in the
# Courtyard (see cli/verb/ask_to_be_led/), so two ways of two steps run through this one person: being
# led to the premises, and following at a distance. Which comes first is the will's own pick; both
# reach the screen, and the third thought has nothing left and says so without proposing. Not "that
# does nothing for it", which is the refusal of an object that was never on the way.
#
# --organs for the noetic points: three thoughts and the opening observation on the kit's own pool
# would not always fit.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --npc-affinity CloseFriend --location-type farm --location-id 1 --start-area "Courtyard" --period afternoon --observe-only "poultry_keeper" --grant-mm bargaining --organs all=5

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

advance 12 180
expect-state will "will bargaining steps=2 first="

click observe "poultry_keeper"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "poultry_keeper"
choose bargaining
advance 12 180
expect-state texts "I must first"

click think "poultry_keeper"
choose bargaining
advance 12 180
expect-state trees ask him to take me to the coop
expect-state trees follow him at a distance
expect-no-state texts "nothing else comes to mind"

click think "poultry_keeper"
choose bargaining
advance 12 180
expect-state texts "nothing else comes to mind"
expect-no-state texts "that does nothing for it"
quit
